[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said the date reports were one issue with one fix queued. The reports
say otherwise. They were merged on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and "wrong date" is a subject that more than one bug produces.

Each problem now has its own ticket, and its reports are merged into it in the ticket export. The
counts below come from the desk's own view of each ticket, so they follow the queue.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It closes <a href="https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1">#1</a>
only. <a href="https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2">#2</a> and
<a href="https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3">#3</a> stay open after it ships.
</Callout>

## #1 · the parser reads day-first dates month first

[Ticket #1](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1). The shared parser reads every
date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.

<CauseTable ticket={1} />

## #2 · booking-v3 tells people to type month first

[Ticket #2](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2). `booking-v3` prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as told, and the form reads the value
the tenant's way. Same symptom as #1, different code, different fix.

<CauseTable ticket={2} />

## #3 · dates move by one day

[Ticket #3](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3). The date moves by one day, not
by a swap: Tuesday becomes Monday, a client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto see different days for
the same meeting, an invite arrives before the booking. That is time-zone handling, not parsing.
By tenant these reports would file under `parser`; the desk read them as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`), and they are filed here.

<CauseTable ticket={3} />

## How a report is placed

1. Count each report once: the export pages overlap, so the same id can appear twice.
2. If the desk read it as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), it goes to #3.
3. Otherwise ask the tenant, not the reporter's browser (`causes.ts`): a day-first tenant on a
   `booking-v3` form goes to #2; every other day-first report goes to #1.

Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser and often names the wrong
cause: compare the "tagged as" column in the tables above.

## For the desk

- Merge into a ticket only reports with the same problem, not the same subject.
- When a new date report comes in, place it with the steps above and merge it into that ticket.
- Do not close the date reports when the parser fix ships; #2 and #3 need their own fixes.

